  "comment": "probe-rs 0.32.0 - Arduino tool definition fragment. PROPOSED, NOT APPROVED: the Windows entries point at an archive re-hosted on this repository, which is an exception to ADR-0002's proposal not to re-host, and neither the ADR nor the exception has been approved. See docs/approval-status.ja.md A-2. The archive is not published yet, so those URLs 404 today; CI serves a locally rebuilt copy instead. What is measured: Linux and macOS tarballs unpack to a single root directory, which is what arduino-cli requires, so those link straight to the probe-rs GitHub Release. The Windows zip is flat - seven files at the root - and arduino-cli refuses it with 'searching package root dir: files in archive must be placed in a subdirectory'. Upstream ships no rooted Windows archive. tools/index/repack_probe_rs.py rebuilds the repacked one byte-for-byte from the upstream archive recorded in upstreamUrl/upstreamChecksum, so it can be verified against upstream by anyone. probe-rs is MIT/Apache-2.0 and both license files travel inside the archive. Sizes and checksums verified 2026-08-20.",
